  `N` (int): A 32-bit integer where the bits will be inserted.
  `M` (int): A 32-bit integer that will be inserted into N.
  `i` (int): The starting bit position (1-based index) where M will be inserted into N.
  `j` (int): The ending bit position (1-based index) where M will be inserted into N.

Output:
  `return` (int): A 32-bit integer representing the result of inserting M into N from bit position i to j.

Given the following output:

1881421453

